  "notes": "Cash basis county, governmental funds only (no business-type funds); CPA-format report. Statement lines from the Government-Wide Total column of the governmental funds statement (p4). Cash and fund balance kept separate: ending cash = Cash at bank 8,562,921 + Cash at bank - restricted 3,019,616 (p3, = printed Total Assets); beginning cash not printed (fund balance 9,006,855 p4 recorded as beginning_fund_balance). Fund-balance roll-forward: 9,006,855 + 10,759,432 - 8,183,750 + 2,516,574 - 2,516,574 = 11,582,537. Balance sheet from the governmental funds statement p3 (totals equal the Statement of Net Position p1; p1 rounds a few restricted lines differently). Taxes 4,853,274 = Statement of Activities 'Property taxes' 4,853,274 (p2), so recorded as property tax (printed tax type beats the Inheritance Tax / Visitor / 911 fund names; review notes added). Intergovernmental 16,532 = Statement of Activities 'In lieu of tax' 16,532 (p2). 'Local' lines kept as other (context label; no exact breakdown). Detail: General Fund budget schedule (p5); Road Bridge Buy Back, Inheritance Tax and Debt Service Bond Fund budget schedules (pp6-7; disbursements printed as one line, function from the p4 fund column); nonmajor funds from the combining statement (pp12-13, one line per fund column; more detailed than the one-line nonmajor budget schedules pp8-11, which are not recorded to avoid double counting). Zero-actual lines (General Fund Federal, Noxious Weed, Road Federal, Veterans Aid fund) omitted. Read pages 1-13 of 13"
}
